# Styling & Theme Guidelines

## Tailwind CSS v4 Configuration

The project uses Tailwind CSS v4 with the new `@theme inline` directive in [src/app/globals.css](mdc:src/app/globals.css).

## Cyberpunk Theme System

The project implements a complete cyberpunk theme with OKLCH color space for consistent theming across both light (Safe Mode) and dark (Cyber Mode) themes.

### Theme Management

- **Package**: `next-themes` for robust theme switching
- **Provider**: [ThemeProvider.tsx](mdc:src/components/ThemeProvider.tsx) wraps the application
- **Toggle**: [ThemeToggle.tsx](mdc:src/components/ThemeToggle.tsx) provides theme switching UI
- **Modes**:
  - **Safe Mode** (Light): Clean, professional, accessible
  - **Cyber Mode** (Dark): Vibrant cyberpunk aesthetic with neon accents

### Color System (OKLCH)

All colors use OKLCH color space for perceptually uniform colors and smooth transitions.

#### Safe Mode (Light Theme)

```css
--primary: oklch(0.45 0.15 280); /* Deep purple */
--secondary: oklch(0.85 0.02 280); /* Light purple-gray */
--accent: oklch(0.65 0.2 160); /* Vibrant green */
--background: oklch(0.98 0.005 280); /* Off-white */
--foreground: oklch(0.15 0.02 280); /* Near black */
--card: oklch(1 0 0); /* Pure white */
--muted: oklch(0.92 0.01 280); /* Soft gray */
--border: oklch(0.85 0.01 280); /* Subtle border */
```

#### Cyber Mode (Dark Theme)

```css
--primary: oklch(0.75 0.25 280); /* Bright electric purple */
--secondary: oklch(0.25 0.05 280); /* Dark purple-gray */
--accent: oklch(0.75 0.25 160); /* Neon green */
--background: oklch(0.1 0.015 280); /* Deep dark purple */
--foreground: oklch(0.95 0.01 280); /* Bright white */
--card: oklch(0.15 0.02 280); /* Dark card */
--muted: oklch(0.25 0.02 280); /* Muted dark */
--border: oklch(0.3 0.05 280); /* Subtle neon border */
```

## Typography System

The project uses a dual-font system for optimal readability and cyberpunk aesthetic.

### Body Text (Geist Sans)

- **Variable**: `--font-geist-sans`
- **Usage**: Body text, UI elements, general content
- **Characteristics**: Clean, modern, highly readable
- **Fallback**: `sans-serif`

### Headings (Rajdhani)

- **Variable**: `--font-rajdhani`
- **Usage**: All headings (h1-h6)
- **Weights**: 300 (Light), 400 (Regular), 500 (Medium), 600 (Semibold), 700 (Bold)
- **Style**: Condensed, geometric, perfect for cyberpunk aesthetic
- **Characteristics**: Sharp, futuristic, attention-grabbing
- **Fallback**: `sans-serif`

```css
h1,
h2,
h3,
h4,
h5,
h6 {
  font-family: var(--font-rajdhani), sans-serif;
  font-weight: 600;
}
```

### Typography Scale

```tsx
// Hero heading
<h1 className="text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-bold">
  Main Heading
</h1>

// Section heading
<h2 className="text-3xl font-bold">Section Title</h2>

// Subsection heading
<h3 className="text-2xl font-semibold">Subsection</h3>

// Card title
<h3 className="text-xl font-semibold">Card Title</h3>

// Body text (standard)
<p className="text-base text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
  Regular body text
</p>

// Body text (large, for important sections)
<p className="text-lg text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
  Important content
</p>

// Small text (metadata, captions)
<p className="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
  Supporting text
</p>
```

## Centralized Color Classes

**CRITICAL: Never use inline opacity modifiers in components (e.g., `bg-muted/50`, `border-primary/20`)**

All color and opacity decisions are centralized in [globals.css](mdc:src/app/globals.css). This prevents color entropy and ensures consistency.

### Background Colors

```tsx
// Standard muted background (50% opacity)
<section className="bg-section-muted">
  Content
</section>

// Subtle background (30% opacity)
<section className="bg-section-subtle">
  Content
</section>

// Accent background (10% opacity)
<section className="bg-section-accent">
  Content
</section>

// Card background (50% opacity)
<Card className="bg-section-card">
  Content
</Card>
```

### Border Colors

```tsx
// Primary border with 20% opacity
<div className="border-2 border-primary-subtle">
  Content
</div>

// Standard border
<div className="border border-section">
  Content
</div>
```

### Hover States

```tsx
// Primary hover effect (transitions to 90% opacity)
<Button className="hover-primary">
  Button Text
</Button>

// Muted hover effect (transitions to 30% opacity)
<div className="hover-muted">
  Interactive Element
</div>
```

### Semantic Colors

Always use semantic Tailwind classes that adapt to the active theme:

```tsx
// Text colors
<p className="text-primary">Primary text</p>
<p className="text-muted-foreground">Secondary text</p>
<p className="text-foreground">Main text</p>
<p className="text-accent">Accent text</p>

// Background colors
<div className="bg-background">Main background</div>
<div className="bg-card">Card background</div>
<div className="bg-muted">Muted background</div>
<div className="bg-primary">Primary background</div>

// Border colors
<div className="border-border">Standard border</div>
<div className="border-primary">Primary border</div>
```

