## Color System Rules

### ✅ DO

- Use standardized classes from `globals.css`: `.bg-section-muted`, `.border-primary-subtle`, etc.
- Use semantic Tailwind classes: `text-primary`, `text-muted-foreground`, `bg-card`
- Define new color patterns in `globals.css` first, then use them in components
- Use CSS variables: `var(--primary)`, `var(--accent)`, etc.
- Test colors in both Safe Mode and Cyber Mode
- Use Rajdhani for all headings, Geist Sans for body text

### ❌ DON'T

- Use inline opacity modifiers: `bg-muted/50`, `border-primary/20`, `text-accent/80`
- Hardcode color values in components: `#a855f7`, `rgb(168, 85, 247)`
- Create ad-hoc color combinations without centralizing them
- Mix hardcoded colors with CSS variables
- Override the font-family for headings (Rajdhani) or body (Geist Sans)

## Color Accessibility

- All colors maintain WCAG AA contrast ratios (4.5:1 for text, 3:1 for UI)
- Safe Mode optimized for readability and accessibility
- Cyber Mode maintains sufficient contrast despite vibrant aesthetics
- Always use semantic color names for clarity
- Test with color blindness simulators
- Verify keyboard navigation works with focus states

## Animation Integration

Combine Tailwind classes with Framer Motion:

```tsx
import { motion } from "framer-motion";

<motion.div
  className="bg-card border border-border rounded-lg p-6"
  whileHover={{
    scale: 1.02,
    boxShadow: "0 0 20px var(--primary)",
  }}
  transition={{ duration: 0.2 }}
>
  Content
</motion.div>;
```

